      "months": 3,
      "stars": 1,
      "text": "Our dachshund stayed at their boarding house for 4 nights. The people working there are really nice, there is no problem with that.\nBUT we brought him home already sick. He is lethargic and coughing. He has an upper respiratory infection (the doctor said so far, but we are going again today because this morning, for example, we couldn't even sleep with him, he was coughing so much) (so he is receiving 3 types of medication). That evening we left the cost of his boarding stay with the vet and now we are going back to the doctor because he is not getting better, so we don't know yet where the amount will end up... (we brought him at 1:00 PM on Friday afternoon, that day he went to the doctor at 6:00 PM and now it is 9:00 AM on Monday morning).\nIf I were to complain to them that this puppy has NEVER been sick, they would definitely explain it. As I'm sure I'll get a response to this post, but I feel like this opinion post is the minimum after all, so that they at least know what they caused us.\n\n/I wrote the exact feeding on the food they gave him, more than half of the amount given was returned. He barely ate for 4 days. He clearly lost weight. In comparison, when I asked by phone how our dog was doing, they always said that he was eating well."
    },
